# Rank 1551 / CVE-2024-27298: Parse Server's Postgres adapter
# escaped quotation marks inside user-supplied $regex query values
# one at a time, so a regex carrying a second quote closed the string
# literal early and injected SQL into the Postgres query (SQL
# injection through an incomplete escape, CWE-89; GHSA-6927-3vr9-
# xf2, fixed in 6.5.3/7.0.0-alpha.20; the pool row's nocommit flag
# was advisory-side absence). literalizeRegexPart in
# src/Adapters/Storage/Postgres/PostgresStorageAdapter.js chained
# `.replace(/([^'])'/, "$1''")` -- no global flag -- so only the
# first quote in the value was doubled; the spec added with the fix
# shows the payload `A'B';SELECT PG_SLEEP(3);--` sailing through the
# escape. Pool commit cbefe770a7 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK by diff
# -- "fix: Improve PostgreSQL injection detection"): the replace
# gains the global flag `(/([^'])'/g, "$1''")` so every quote in the
# value is escaped. No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, escape-completeness inside a sanitizer. The escaping
# helper exists and runs -- its defect is that a non-global replace
# handles only the first match, the same present-but-incomplete
# family as ranks 1564 (pgjdbc's unquoted bind types) and 1522
# (bracket-blind hosts): nothing can ask "does this string-replace
# sanitize every occurrence in the value" -- regex-flag semantics on
# a project-local helper are not observed by any rule. A binding on
# Parse Server's own literalizeRegexPart would detect this
# application rather than the weakness. Measured on the real code:
# scanning PostgresStorageAdapter.js reports zero findings at both
# revisions (the injection crosses through the adapter's own query
# assembly, a project-API boundary). No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: the
# piece is replace-completeness vocabulary, not a localised
# construct. No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1551
# records the single-shot escape and the global-flag form, both
# asserting reject VYQL-INJ-001: when replace-completeness
# vocabulary lands, the single-shot form must flip to expect.

test "rank1551: the regex quote escape stops at the first match"
  lang javascript
  file src/Adapters/Storage/Postgres/PostgresStorageAdapter.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  function literalizeRegexPart(s) {
    return s
      .replace(/([\f\n\r\t\v])/g, `\\${'$1'}`)
      .replace(/([^\\])(\\Q)/, '$1')
      .replace(/^\\E/, '')
      .replace(/^\\Q/, '')
      .replace(/([^'])'/, `$1''`)
      .replace(/^'([^'])/, `''$1`);
  }

  function buildRegexClause(column, regexValue) {
    const literal = literalizeRegexPart(regexValue);
    return `WHERE ${column} ~ '${literal}'`;
  }
  ```

test "rank1551: the fix escapes every quote in the value"
  lang javascript
  file src/Adapters/Storage/Postgres/PostgresStorageAdapter.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  function literalizeRegexPart(s) {
    return s
      .replace(/([\f\n\r\t\v])/g, `\\${'$1'}`)
      .replace(/([^\\])(\\Q)/, '$1')
      .replace(/^\\E/, '')
      .replace(/^\\Q/, '')
      .replace(/([^'])'/g, `$1''`)
      .replace(/^'([^'])/, `''$1`);
  }

  function buildRegexClause(column, regexValue) {
    const literal = literalizeRegexPart(regexValue);
    return `WHERE ${column} ~ '${literal}'`;
  }
